{"batchcomplete": true, "query": {"redirects": [{"from": "Kuelap", "to": "Kuélap"}], "pages": [{"pageid": 321908, "ns": 0, "title": "King asleep in mountain", "extract": "The king asleep in the mountain (D 1960.2 in Stith Thompson's motif-index) is a prominent folklore trope found in many folktales and legends. Thompson termed it as the Kyffhäuser type. Some other designations are king in the mountain, king under the mountain, sleeping hero, or Bergentrückung (\"mountain rapture\").\nExamples include the legends of King Arthur, Fionn mac Cumhaill, Charlemagne, Ogier the Dane, King David, Frederick Barbarossa at Kyffhäuser, Falanto of Taranto, Genghis Khan, Constantine XI Palaiologos, Kraljević Marko, Sebastian of Portugal and King Matjaž.\nThe Thompson motif entries A 571, \"Cultural hero asleep in mountain\", and E 502, \"The Sleeping Army\", are similar and can occur in the same tale. A related motif is the \"Seven Sleepers\" (D 1960.1, also known as the \"Rip Van Winkle\" motif), whose type tale is the Seven Sleepers of Ephesus (AT tale type 766).", "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2026-08-06T17:44:38Z", "lastrevid": 1367028710, "length": 40401, "fullurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_asleep_in_mountain", "editurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=King_asleep_in_mountain&action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_asleep_in_mountain", "pageprops": {"wikibase_item": "Q1131291"}, "extlinks": [{"url": "http://www.pitt.edu/~dash/sleep.html"}, {"url": "http://gutenberg.spiegel.de/grimm/sagen/g028.htm"}, {"url": "http://members.tripod.com/alabasters_archive/canaanism_solutions.html"}, {"url": "http://www.benyehuda.org/bialik/veyehi_hayom_hamelex_david_bameara.html"}, {"url": "http://www.hums.canterbury.ac.nz/clas/ejms/out_of_print/JMSv1n2/JMSv1n2Boyle.pdf"}, {"url": "https://books.google.com/books?id=PIuLBDOUc80C&pg=PA85"}, {"url": "https://books.google.com/books?id=WpDJObx8lpMC&pg=PA83"}, {"url": "https://books.google.com/books?id=KEcsAQAAIAAJ&q=%221960.2%22"}, {"url": "https://www.jstor.org/stable/20522387"}, {"url": "https://books.google.com/books?id=vxvaAAAAMAAJ"}, {"url": "https://books.google.com/books?id=lkqIalGZwZgC&pg=PA143"}, {"url": "https://books.google.com/books?id=-_8hAQAAMAAJ&q=D%C3%B3nall"}, {"url": "https://doi.org/10.3986/sms.v2i0.1848"}, {"url": "https://tatromaniak.pl/aktualnosci/legenda-o-spiacych-rycerzach/"}, {"url": "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/nation/2021/11/02/texas-qanon-believers-back-theory-trump-reinstated/6255234001/"}, {"url": "https://doi.org/10.2307%2F20522387"}, {"url": "https://doi.org/10.2307%2F20522397"}, {"url": "https://www.jstor.org/stable/20522397"}, {"url": "https://doi.org/10.2307%2F20522558"}, {"url": "https://www.jstor.org/stable/20522558"}, {"url": "https://books.google.com/books?id=lkqIalGZwZgC&dq=Bishop+Melchisedech+of+Roumania+Slavonic+sect+Napoleon&pg=PA144"}, {"url": "https://books.google.com/books?id=H5pyUIY4THYC"}, {"url": "https://www.snopes.com/fact-check/suspended-animation/"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20210123132948/https://www.snopes.com/fact-check/suspended-animation/"}, {"url": "https://www.mitologia.pt/a-batalha-de-guadalete-e-o-destino-do-539701"}, {"url": "https://www.mitologia.pt/a-origem-do-sebastianismo-590784"}, {"url": "https://www.amazon.com/Famous-Legends-Portugal-Portuguese-presented-ebook/dp/B09DFRTVKB/"}, {"url": "https://czv.897.myftpupload.com/georgias-queen-of-kings-tamar-the-great/"}, {"url": "http://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/0015587X.1986.9716380"}, {"url": "https://doi.org/10.1080%2F0015587X.1986.9716380"}, {"url": "https://search.worldcat.org/issn/0015-587X"}, {"url": "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1257717"}, {"url": "https://doi.org/10.1080%2F0015587X.1952.9718105"}, {"url": "https://doi.org/10.2307%2F20521720"}, {"url": "https://www.jstor.org/stable/20521720"}, {"url": "https://d.lib.rochester.edu/camelot/text/pollock-merlin-and-vivien"}, {"url": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Mount-Koya"}, {"url": "https://doi.org/10.35308%2Fijelr.v5i1.7504"}, {"url": "https://search.worldcat.org/issn/1949-8519"}, {"url": "https://search.worldcat.org/issn/2721-4273"}, {"url": "https://unitesi.unive.it/bitstream/20.500.14247/2081/1/805414-1161230.pdf"}, {"url": "https://d1wqtxts1xzle7.cloudfront.net/58283823/oroz_skrbic_heroic_topography-libre.pdf?1548759541=&response-content-disposition=inline%3B+filename%3DHeroic_Topographies_Hero_making_and_Plac.pdf&Expires=1746351767&Signature=P17VoKW~S8YeibNNYhpt3As20sDOKmhniL6kfnMaMsrA22FT4BWLw1QJ0nqmSFClnRCkUSQX6hSmcRpZ7ItWUKKg3Vz6obIKc3XG55sYpBenz01E9igildsdKqHxVR2g6kNrqh6D9OCjwiObMNT4cwBJeW1bHGcRsv-EP6ZCQGGun~7T~ApdPpkZ7sjRaIJ7Iqo7vjBMWrbSOaUMf0iGWbwJfua1uij5BkLWOse6khAFVqyF4U82-m-nPAEKsiuMvEOHlvxUh0TDcrgUgTSvUN~RgX5c-DnK2efqVYa8frX4u8l79Sw2IjD08z9KtkduPqrO2w6ZUdiaoqx0Bh13cg__&Key-Pair-Id=APKAJLOHF5GGSLRBV4ZA"}, {"url": "https://www.fwls.org/uploads/soft/190810/1-1ZQ0130601.pdf#page=75"}, {"url": "http://jurnal.utu.ac.id/IJELR/article/view/7504"}, {"url": "https://books.google.com/books?id=JE4LAAAAIAAJ"}, {"url": "https://books.google.com/books?id=a-fDCQAAQBAJ&dq=Gesar+of+Ling+return&pg=PR7"}, {"url": "https://doi.org/10.1080%2F0015587X.1949.9717929"}, {"url": "https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/pdf/10.1080/0015587X.1949.9717929"}, {"url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pcamjcoRmrQ"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20100602115916/http://www.hums.canterbury.ac.nz/clas/ejms/out_of_print/JMSv1n2/JMSv1n2Boyle.pdf"}, {"url": "https://pravoslavie.ru/28069.html"}, {"url": "https://books.google.com/books?id=OgMmceadQ3gC&dq=Kalki+encyclopedia&pg=PA223"}, {"url": "https://shs.cairn.info/frederic-ii--9782262049829-page-299"}, {"url": "https://doi.org/10.37547%2Ftajssei%2FVolume03Issue01-93"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20210716073229/https://www.usajournalshub.com/index.php/tajssei/article/download/2038/1941/"}, {"url": "https://www.summitpost.org/page/153793"}, {"url": "https://mouseplanet.com/walt-disney-was-not-frozen/6095/"}, {"url": "https://www.sfgate.com/disneyland/article/Walt-Disney-head-isnt-really-frozen-16526600.php"}]}, {"pageid": 3152860, "ns": 0, "title": "Kuntur Wasi", "extract": "Kuntur Wasi (Quechua kuntur condor, wasi house, \"condor house\") is the name given to the ruins of a religious center with complex architecture and stone sculptures, located in the Andean highlands of Peru. It is believed the inhabitants had a link with the Chavín culture.\nKuntur Wasi is located on La Copa hill in the northern Andean highlands of Peru, in the San Pablo Province of the Cajamarca Region, near the village of Kuntur Wasi (formerly known as La Conga). The site is roughly 2,300 meters above sea level. The architecture consists of a hill-top temple, quadrangular platforms, a sunken courtyard, and series of rooms.", "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2026-08-06T02:43:10Z", "lastrevid": 1365403194, "length": 8347, "fullurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kuntur_Wasi", "editurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Kuntur_Wasi&action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kuntur_Wasi", "pageprops": {"wikibase_item": "Q1792721"}, "coordinates": [{"lat": -7.12944444, "lon": -78.84527778, "primary": true, "globe": "earth"}], "extlinks": [{"url": "http://www.i-m.mx/Museo/KunturWasi/"}, {"url": "https://futatraw.ourproject.org/descargas/DicQuechuaBolivia.pdf"}, {"url": "https://geohack.toolforge.org/geohack.php?pagename=Kuntur_Wasi&params=07_07_46_S_78_50_43_W_"}, {"url": "https://geohack.toolforge.org/geohack.php?pagename=Kuntur_Wasi&params=07_07_46_S_78_50_43_W_type:landmark"}, {"url": "https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1111/1468-0033.00229"}, {"url": "https://kuprimo.hosted.exlibrisgroup.com/permalink/f/mfn9op/TN_cdi_gale_infotracmisc_A307526633"}]}, {"pageid": 6136903, "ns": 0, "title": "Kuélap", "extract": "Kuélap or Cuélap is a walled settlement located in the mountains near the towns of María and Tingo, in the southern part of the region of Amazonas, Peru. It was built by the Chachapoyas culture in the 6th century AD on a ridge overlooking the Utcubamba Valley.\n\n", "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2026-08-06T02:43:39Z", "lastrevid": 1365247786, "length": 15548, "fullurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ku%C3%A9lap", "editurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ku%C3%A9lap&action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ku%C3%A9lap", "pageprops": {"wikibase_item": "Q1361820"}, "coordinates": [{"lat": -6.426295, "lon": -77.9271134, "primary": true, "globe": "earth"}], "extlinks": [{"url": "http://ficha.sigmincetur.mincetur.gob.pe/index.aspx?cod_Ficha=754"}, {"url": "https://www.wmf.org/project/kuelap-fortress"}, {"url": "https://whc.unesco.org/en/tentativelists/5650/"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20170905004725/http://ficha.sigmincetur.mincetur.gob.pe/index.aspx?cod_Ficha=754"}, {"url": "https://andina.pe/Ingles/noticia-peru-cablecar-system-to-bring-over-75000-visitors-to-kuelap-this-year-656292.aspx"}, {"url": "https://books.google.com/books?id=ILnxAgAAQBAJ"}, {"url": "https://books.google.com/books?id=AX5xAAAAMAAJ&q=Juan+Cris%C3%B3stomo+Nieto,+a+Chachapoyas+judge"}, {"url": "https://doi.org/10.1080%2F00934690.2020.1713287"}, {"url": "https://geohack.toolforge.org/geohack.php?pagename=Ku%C3%A9lap&params=6.426295_S_77.9271134_W_"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20111019161551/http://kuelapvirtual.com/"}, {"url": "https://www.kuelap.city/"}, {"url": "https://andina.pe/agencia/noticia-peru-new-discovery-reveals-funerary-structure-with-ceremonial-offerings-in-kuelap-1076181.aspx"}, {"url": "https://greekreporter.com/2025/05/21/ancient-tomb-offerings-peru-kuelap-city/"}]}, {"pageid": 16306451, "ns": 0, "title": "Killke culture", "extract": "The Killke culture occupied the South American region around Cusco, Peru, from 900 to 1200 AD, prior to the development of Incan culture in the 13th century.\nKillke culture flourished in highland Peru in the Late Intermediate Period around what is now Cusco. Archaeologist Oscar Rodriguez suggests that the Killke built small sections of the fortress Saksaywaman during the 12th century, prior to the Incan expansion of the site.\nIn 2008, excavations uncovered a temple on the edge of the fortress, indicating religious as well as military use of the site.\nJohn H. Rowe first described killke ceramics. These vessels are often globular with vertical strap handles and have simple linear geometric decorations of black or black-on-red over a white or buff slip.\nIt was the American archaeologist John Howland Rowe (1918–2004) who named the Killke culture.", "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2026-08-06T17:50:28Z", "lastrevid": 1350772565, "length": 8088, "fullurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Killke_culture", "editurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Killke_culture&action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Killke_culture", "pageprops": {"wikibase_item": "Q6407873"}, "extlinks": [{"url": "http://edition.cnn.com/2008/TECH/03/15/peru.temple.ap/index.html"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20111113233438/http://www.goodprovenance.com/incapots.htm"}, {"url": "https://books.google.com/books?id=TWLjONT3uYQC&pg=PA74"}, {"url": "https://www.nbcnews.com/id/wbna23626672"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20081105082006/http://edition.cnn.com/2008/TECH/03/15/peru.temple.ap/index.html"}, {"url": "http://www.comcast.net/news/index.jsp?cat=GENERAL&fn=/2008/03/14/911994.html"}]}, {"pageid": 22807112, "ns": 0, "title": "Kuhikugu", "extract": "Kuhikugu is an archaeological site located in Brazil, at the headwaters of the Xingu River, in the Amazon rainforest. The area around Kuhikugu is located in part of the Xingu National Park today. Kuhikugu was first uncovered by anthropologist Michael Heckenberger, working alongside the local Kuikuro people, who are the likely descendants of the original inhabitants of Kuhikugu.", "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2026-08-06T17:52:01Z", "lastrevid": 1322059294, "length": 7060, "fullurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kuhikugu", "editurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Kuhikugu&action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kuhikugu", "pageprops": {"wikibase_item": "Q6442109"}, "coordinates": [{"lat": -12.55833333, "lon": -53.11111111, "primary": true, "globe": "earth"}], "extlinks": [{"url": "http://plaza.ufl.edu/duin/Xtra/AMAZONIA%201492.%20HECKENBERGER.htm"}, {"url": "https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/lost-amazon-cities/"}, {"url": "https://books.google.com/books?id=hAKratAxR18C&q=%22Kuhikugu,+which+means%22&pg=PA95"}, {"url": "https://books.google.com/books?id=QPih33JBeMwC&q=editions:mjUTYzplSmcC"}, {"url": "https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/lost-amazon-cities"}, {"url": "https://geohack.toolforge.org/geohack.php?pagename=Kuhikugu&params=12_33_30_S_53_6_40_W_type:landmark_region:BR"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20110523102327/http://plaza.ufl.edu/duin/Xtra/AMAZONIA%201492.%20HECKENBERGER.htm"}]}, {"pageid": 25187408, "ns": 0, "title": "Kotosh", "extract": "Kotosh is an archaeological site near the town of Huánuco, Peru, consisting of a series of buildings comprising six periods of continuous occupation.\n\n", "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2026-08-06T02:45:58Z", "lastrevid": 1364839908, "length": 6575, "fullurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kotosh", "editurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Kotosh&action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kotosh", "pageprops": {"wikibase_item": "Q2669852"}, "coordinates": [{"lat": -9.93083333, "lon": -76.27944444, "primary": true, "globe": "earth"}], "extlinks": [{"url": "http://www.veperu.com/turismo/turismo-peru/1224938939/huanuco.php"}, {"url": "http://www.um.u-tokyo.ac.jp/publish_db/Bulletin/no03/no03003.html"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20030113175943/http://www.um.u-tokyo.ac.jp/publish_db/Bulletin/no03/no03003.html"}, {"url": "http://ficha.sigmincetur.mincetur.gob.pe/index.aspx?cod_Ficha=683"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20100101163453/http://www.veperu.com/turismo/turismo-peru/1224938939/huanuco.php"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20090512153146/http://wiki.sumaqperu.com/es/Kotosh"}, {"url": "https://books.google.com/books?id=BDKqBgAAQBAJ&pg=PT552"}, {"url": "https://geohack.toolforge.org/geohack.php?pagename=Kotosh&params=9_55_51_S_76_16_46_W_region:PE_type:landmark_source:kolossus-ltwiki"}, {"url": "https://doi.org/10.1017%2Flaq.2020.89"}, {"url": "https://search.worldcat.org/issn/1045-6635"}, {"url": "http://www.absolut-peru.com/templo-de-las-manos-cruzadas-de-kotosh/"}]}, {"pageid": 32035302, "ns": 0, "title": "La Centinela", "extract": "La Centinela is an archaeological site in Peru which was an active administrative center during both the Inca and pre-Inca periods.", "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2026-08-06T17:54:23Z", "lastrevid": 1364840275, "length": 3803, "fullurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Centinela", "editurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=La_Centinela&action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Centinela", "pageprops": {"wikibase_item": "Q6461630"}, "coordinates": [{"lat": -13.45027778, "lon": -76.17111111, "primary": true, "globe": "earth"}], "extlinks": [{"url": "https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusID:131557376"}, {"url": "https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusID:163186881"}, {"url": "https://doi.org/10.1086%2Fsoutjanth.15.2.3628802"}, {"url": "https://doi.org/10.2307%2F276783"}, {"url": "https://www.jstor.org/stable/276783"}, {"url": "https://geohack.toolforge.org/geohack.php?pagename=La_Centinela&params=13_27_1_S_76_10_16_W_"}, {"url": "https://geohack.toolforge.org/geohack.php?pagename=La_Centinela&params=13_27_1_S_76_10_16_W_type:landmark"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20110830091147/https://sweetpotatoknowledge.org/sweetpotato-introduction/history/Archeology%20remains%20of%20sweetpotato%20and%20potato%20in%20Peru.pdf?set_language=pt&cl=pt"}, {"url": "https://sweetpotatoknowledge.org/sweetpotato-introduction/history/Archeology%20remains%20of%20sweetpotato%20and%20potato%20in%20Peru.pdf?set_language=pt&cl=pt"}]}, {"pageid": 33650400, "ns": 0, "title": "Kotosh Religious Tradition", "extract": "The Kotosh Religious Tradition is a term used by archaeologists to refer to the ritual buildings that were constructed in the mountain drainages of the Peruvian Andes between circa 3000 and c. 1800 BCE, during the Andean preceramic, or Late Archaic period of Andean history.\n\nArchaeologists have identified and excavated a number of these ritual centers; the first of these to be discovered was that at Kotosh, although since then further examples have been found at Shillacoto, Wairajirca, Huaricoto, La Galgada, Piruru, among others. These sites are all located in highland zones that are lower than the Puna, and yet there are considerable distances separating them. In spite of this, all these cases of highland preceramic public architecture are remarkably similar.\nKotosh tradition shows numerous links with the Chavín culture that emerged at most of these sites subsequently.", "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2026-08-06T17:54:50Z", "lastrevid": 1307890465, "length": 10711, "fullurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kotosh_Religious_Tradition", "editurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Kotosh_Religious_Tradition&action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kotosh_Religious_Tradition", "pageprops": {"wikibase_item": "Q6434200"}, "extlinks": [{"url": "http://www.um.u-tokyo.ac.jp/publish_db/Bulletin/no03/no03003.html"}, {"url": "http://www.utexas.edu/courses/arh400/lectures/347/arhreview1.htm"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20030113175943/http://www.um.u-tokyo.ac.jp/publish_db/Bulletin/no03/no03003.html"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20110707075418/http://www.absolut-peru.com/templo-de-las-manos-cruzadas-de-kotosh/"}]}, {"pageid": 41731996, "ns": 0, "title": "Kenko, Puno", "extract": "\\\n\nKenko, Qenqo or Q'inq'u (possibly Aymara for \"twisted, bent\") or also Inka Anatawi, is an archaeological site in Peru. It is located in the Puno Region, Puno Province, Acora District, at an elevation of about 4,000 m (13,000 ft). The site was declared a National Cultural Heritage (Patrimonio Cultural) of Peru by the National Institute of Culture.", "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2026-08-06T17:56:41Z", "lastrevid": 1364715327, "length": 2775, "fullurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kenko,_Puno", "editurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Kenko,_Puno&action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kenko,_Puno", "pageprops": {"wikibase_item": "Q15949971"}, "extlinks": [{"url": "http://www.mincetur.gob.pe/TURISMO/OTROS/inventario%20turistico/Ficha.asp?cod_Ficha=5018"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20140204053051/http://www.mincetur.gob.pe/TURISMO/OTROS/inventario%20turistico/Ficha.asp?cod_Ficha=5018"}]}, {"pageid": 41788937, "ns": 0, "title": "Khapia", "extract": "Khapia (possibly from in the Aymara spelling Qhapiya, or Qapiya in Uru language, Hispanicized spellings Capía, Ccapia, Ccapía, Khapia, Khapía, K'apía) is a mountain in Peru, possibly an extinct volcano,  situated at a height of about 4,809 metres (15,778 ft). It is located in the Puno Region, Chucuito Province, in the districts Pomata and Zepita, and in the Yunguyo Province, in the districts Cuturapi, Copani and Yunguyo. The mountain lies near Lake Titicaca at the road which connects Yunguyo and Puno, south of the hill Asiru Phat'jata.\nIn 2011 Khapia with its prehispanic archaeological site was declared a National Cultural Heritage (Patrimonio Cultural) of Peru by resolution No. 589-2011-VMPCIC-MC of May 13, 2011, of the Vice Minister of the Ministry of Culture and a \"Landscape Reserve\" (Zona de Reserva Paisajística in Spanish) by Decrete Supreme No. 008-2011-MINAM.\nBy the local people the mountain is venerated as an Apu.", "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2026-08-06T02:47:31Z", "lastrevid": 1355456870, "length": 4192, "fullurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khapia", "editurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Khapia&action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khapia", "pageprops": {"wikibase_item": "Q5763064"}, "coordinates": [{"lat": -16.33119444, "lon": -69.14227778, "primary": true, "globe": "earth"}], "extlinks": [{"url": "http://www.mincetur.gob.pe/TURISMO/OTROS/inventario%20turistico/Ficha.asp?cod_Ficha=4712"}, {"url": "http://mapcarta.com/20235812"}, {"url": "http://biblio.perueduca.edu.pe/documentos/cdapoyo/Libros/Aymara/"}, {"url": "http://www.illa-a.org/cd/diccionarios/VocabularioUru-Hannss-output.html"}, {"url": "http://geodeg.com/search.php?q=volcano&language=24&country=&n=780"}, {"url": "http://www.regionpuno.gob.pe/web/archives/2041"}, {"url": "http://www.cepes.org.pe/apc-aa/archivos-aa/4a15e4303d8c04dde2018292e444138c/DS_008_2011.pdf"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20140218210325/http://www.mincetur.gob.pe/TURISMO/OTROS/inventario%20turistico/Ficha.asp?cod_Ficha=4712"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20140202120107/http://biblio.perueduca.edu.pe/documentos/cdapoyo/Libros/Aymara/"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20140203025706/http://www.regionpuno.gob.pe/web/archives/2041"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20150923201913/http://www.cepes.org.pe/apc-aa/archivos-aa/4a15e4303d8c04dde2018292e444138c/DS_008_2011.pdf"}, {"url": "https://geohack.toolforge.org/geohack.php?pagename=Khapia&params=16_19_52.3_S_69_08_32.2_W_type:mountain_region:PE_scale:100000"}]}, {"pageid": 42042504, "ns": 0, "title": "Killarumiyuq", "extract": "Killarumiyuq (Quechua killa moon, rumi stone, -yuq a suffix to indicate ownership, \"the one with a moon stone\", Hispanicized and mixed spellings Killarumiyoc, Quillarumiyoc, Quillarumiyoq, also Killarumiyoq) is an archaeological park in Peru. It is located in the Cusco Region, Anta Province, Ancahuasi District. The site was declared a National Cultural Heritage (Patrimonio Cultural) of Peru by Resolución Directoral Nacional No. 150/INC-2003 of March 25, 2003.", "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2026-08-06T17:56:46Z", "lastrevid": 1364715613, "length": 2179, "fullurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Killarumiyuq", "editurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Killarumiyuq&action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Killarumiyuq", "pageprops": {"wikibase_item": "Q17074808"}, "coordinates": [{"lat": -13.44520556, "lon": -72.30992778, "primary": true, "globe": "earth"}], "extlinks": [{"url": "http://www.mincetur.gob.pe/TURISMO/OTROS/inventario%20turistico/Ficha.asp?cod_Ficha=3125"}, {"url": "https://geohack.toolforge.org/geohack.php?pagename=Killarumiyuq&params=13_26_42.74_S_72_18_35.74_W_region:PE_type:landmark_dim:20"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20160303230255/http://www.mincetur.gob.pe/TURISMO/OTROS/inventario%20turistico/Ficha.asp?cod_Ficha=3125"}]}, {"pageid": 42233521, "ns": 0, "title": "Khichuqaqa", "extract": "Khichuqaqa (Quechua khichu a piece of a whole, fraction, qaqa rock, also spelled K'echuqaqa) is an archaeological site in Peru with rock paintings and tombs nearby. It is situated in the Cusco Region, Urubamba Province, Urubamba District. The site lies at a height of about 3,160 metres (10,367 ft) on the slope of the mountain Kapuliyuq (Quechua for \"the one with the bitter-berry tree\", Capulliyoq).", "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2026-08-06T17:56:48Z", "lastrevid": 1364838955, "length": 1865, "fullurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khichuqaqa", "editurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Khichuqaqa&action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khichuqaqa", "pageprops": {"wikibase_item": "Q17074797"}}, {"pageid": 42264299, "ns": 0, "title": "Kunturmarka, Pasco", "extract": "Kunturmarka (Quechua kuntur condor, marka village / storey, Hispanicized spelling Condormarca) is an archaeological site in Peru. It is situated in the Pasco Region, Pasco Province, Paucartambo District. The complex consists of round buildings and stone tombs (chullpa).", "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2026-08-06T17:56:49Z", "lastrevid": 1364715869, "length": 2216, "fullurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kunturmarka,_Pasco", "editurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Kunturmarka,_Pasco&action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kunturmarka,_Pasco", "pageprops": {"wikibase_item": "Q17074955"}, "extlinks": [{"url": "http://www.mincetur.gob.pe/TURISMO/OTROS/inventario%20turistico/Ficha.asp?cod_Ficha=876"}]}, {"pageid": 42267116, "ns": 0, "title": "Kukuli, Arequipa", "extract": "Kukuli (Quechua for white-winged dove) is an archaeological site with rock paintings and tombs in Peru. It is located in the Arequipa Region, Caravelí Province, Caravelí District.", "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2026-08-06T17:56:49Z", "lastrevid": 1364840020, "length": 1951, "fullurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kukuli,_Arequipa", "editurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Kukuli,_Arequipa&action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kukuli,_Arequipa", "pageprops": {"wikibase_item": "Q15991587"}, "extlinks": [{"url": "http://www.mincetur.gob.pe/TURISMO/OTROS/inventario%20turistico/Ficha.asp?cod_Ficha=2763"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20140322001925/http://www.mincetur.gob.pe/TURISMO/OTROS/inventario%20turistico/Ficha.asp?cod_Ficha=2763"}]}, {"pageid": 42367862, "ns": 0, "title": "Kunturmarka, Ayacucho", "extract": "Kunturmarka (Quechua kuntur condor, marka village / storey, Hispanicized spelling Condormarca) is an archaeological site in Peru. It is situated in the Ayacucho Region, Huanta Province, Huamanguilla District.", "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2026-08-06T17:56:50Z", "lastrevid": 1364715859, "length": 2030, "fullurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kunturmarka,_Ayacucho", "editurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Kunturmarka,_Ayacucho&action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kunturmarka,_Ayacucho", "pageprops": {"wikibase_item": "Q17074944"}}, {"pageid": 42752683, "ns": 0, "title": "Kuntuyuq", "extract": "Kuntuyuq or Quntuyuq (Quechua kuntu, quntu fragrance, aroma, -yuq a suffix, \"the one with a fragrance\", Hispanicized spelling Contuyog, Cuntuyog) is an archaeological site with rock paintings on a mountain of the same name in Peru. It lies in the Pasco Region, Daniel Alcides Carrion Province, Chacayan District, in the community of Iskayqucha (Quechua for \"two lakes\", Hispanicized Iscaycocha), north-west of the lake Allqaqucha. The mountain rises up to  4,475 metres (14,682 ft) above sea level. The archaeological site of Kuntuyuq is situated at a height of about 4,433 metres (14,544 ft).", "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2026-08-06T02:47:35Z", "lastrevid": 1364715875, "length": 2548, "fullurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kuntuyuq", "editurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Kuntuyuq&action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kuntuyuq", "pageprops": {"wikibase_item": "Q17074979"}, "coordinates": [{"lat": -10.54944444, "lon": -76.35916667, "primary": true, "globe": "earth"}], "extlinks": [{"url": "http://www.mincetur.gob.pe/TURISMO/OTROS/inventario%20turistico/Ficha.asp?cod_Ficha=6958"}, {"url": "http://www.mincetur.gob.pe/TURISMO/OTROS/inventario%20turistico/Ficha.asp?cod_Ficha=6980"}, {"url": "https://geohack.toolforge.org/geohack.php?pagename=Kuntuyuq&params=10_32_58_S_76_21_33_W_"}, {"url": "https://geohack.toolforge.org/geohack.php?pagename=Kuntuyuq&params=10_32_58_S_76_21_33_W_type:landmark"}]}, {"pageid": 42799487, "ns": 0, "title": "Kuntur Amaya", "extract": "Kuntur Amaya (Spanish: Cóndor Amaya) is an archaeological site in Bolivia. It is located in the La Paz Department, Aroma Province, Umala Municipality, near Wayllani (Huayllani). The site was declared a National Monument on December 12, 2006. The site contains chullpas (Aymara funerary towers).", "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2026-08-06T02:47:36Z", "lastrevid": 1364840083, "length": 2769, "fullurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kuntur_Amaya", "editurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Kuntur_Amaya&action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kuntur_Amaya", "pageprops": {"wikibase_item": "Q17074933"}, "coordinates": [{"lat": -17.325, "lon": -68.09722222, "primary": true, "globe": "earth"}], "extlinks": [{"url": "https://geohack.toolforge.org/geohack.php?pagename=Kuntur_Amaya&params=17_19_30_S_68_05_50_W_"}, {"url": "https://geohack.toolforge.org/geohack.php?pagename=Kuntur_Amaya&params=17_19_30_S_68_05_50_W_type:landmark"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20140519112129/https://www.lostiempos.com/oh/actualidad/actualidad/20110206/media_recortes/2011/02/03/219678_gd.jpg"}, {"url": "https://www.lexivox.org/norms/BO-L-3597.xhtml"}, {"url": "https://www.rfi.fr/en/contenu/20190602-bolivia-restores-myth-generating-funerary-towers"}, {"url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1296207423001371"}, {"url": "https://doi.org/10.1016%2Fj.culher.2023.07.015"}, {"url": "https://search.worldcat.org/issn/1296-2074"}]}, {"pageid": 46295424, "ns": 0, "title": "Kanichi, Peru", "extract": "Kanichi  (from Ayacucho Quechua, Hispanicized spelling Caniche) is an archaeological site in Peru. It was declared a National Cultural Heritage by RDN No. 197/INC on April 2, 2003. Kanichi lies in the Ayacucho Region, Lucanas Province, Carmen Salcedo District.\nThe archaeological complex, which is about 200,000 square meters, was influenced by the Wari and Chanka cultures. The complex includes a variety of buildings including Chullpas, religious and ceremonial buildings, service centers, and a water system of wells and springs.\nKanichi is open to tourists from 6am to 6pm.", "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2026-08-06T17:57:48Z", "lastrevid": 1364838515, "length": 2533, "fullurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kanichi,_Peru", "editurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Kanichi,_Peru&action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kanichi,_Peru", "pageprops": {"wikibase_item": "Q13189747"}, "coordinates": [{"lat": -14.38416667, "lon": -73.95722222, "primary": true, "globe": "earth"}], "extlinks": [{"url": "http://www.mincetur.gob.pe/turismo/OTROS/inventario%20turistico/Ficha.asp?cod_Ficha=1267"}, {"url": "https://turismoi.pe/arqueologia/sitio-arqueologico/complejo-arqueologico-de-caniche.htm"}, {"url": "https://indigenasdelperu.files.wordpress.com/2015/09/diccionario-qeswa-academia-mayor-cuzco.pdf"}, {"url": "https://geohack.toolforge.org/geohack.php?pagename=Kanichi,_Peru&params=14_23_03_S_73_57_26_W_"}, {"url": "https://geohack.toolforge.org/geohack.php?pagename=Kanichi,_Peru&params=14_23_03_S_73_57_26_W_type:landmark"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20160304103749/http://www.mincetur.gob.pe/turismo/OTROS/inventario%20turistico/Ficha.asp?cod_Ficha=1267"}]}, {"pageid": 47591837, "ns": 0, "title": "Killa Mach'ay", "extract": "Killa Mach'ay (Quechua killa moon, mach'ay cave, \"moon cave\", also spelled Killa Machay, Killamachay, Quillamachay) is an archaeological site with rock paintings and petroglyphs in Peru. It is situated in the Huancavelica Region, Acobamba Province, Acobamba District. The site consists of caves with images of llamas, lines and people. It is situated at a height of 3,400 metres (11,155 ft).", "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2026-08-06T17:58:10Z", "lastrevid": 1364839116, "length": 2077, "fullurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Killa_Mach%27ay", "editurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Killa_Mach%27ay&action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Killa_Mach%27ay", "pageprops": {"wikibase_item": "Q21044255"}, "extlinks": [{"url": "http://www.mincetur.gob.pe/TURISMO/OTROS/inventario%20turistico/Ficha.asp?cod_Ficha=4281"}, {"url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20160304103735/http://www.mincetur.gob.pe/TURISMO/OTROS/inventario%20turistico/Ficha.asp?cod_Ficha=4281"}, {"url": "https://futatraw.ourproject.org/descargas/DicQuechuaBolivia.pdf"}]}]}, "limits": {"coordinates": 500, "extlinks": 500}}